From: Chloe <chloeq231@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] init: allow opted-in recovery reboot without a misc partition

Samsung grandppltedx selects recovery using sec_reboot's reason, not a BCB.
The Android 11 mandatory BCB write otherwise aborts the reboot before shutdown.
Default to the existing BCB behavior; skip only for an explicit device property
and the plain recovery target. Other targets and BCB failure handling stay intact.

--- a/init/reboot.cpp
+++ b/init/reboot.cpp
@@ -990,7 +990,8 @@
                                   "bootloader_message: "
                                << err;
                 }
-            } else if (reboot_target == "recovery") {
+            } else if (reboot_target == "recovery" &&
+                       !GetBoolProperty("ro.vendor.recovery.skip_bcb", false)) {
                 bootloader_message boot = {};
                 if (std::string err; !read_bootloader_message(&boot, &err)) {
                     LOG(ERROR) << "Failed to read bootloader message: " << err;
